  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 108 PM MDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nFor Wednesday and Thursday, it will likely be dry over the \nregion. Any storms, if they form, will be isolated at best. \nTemperatures will warm up a bit as compared to today, with \ngenerally mid 90s over the plains and around 90 over the divides \n(Palmer and Raton). Over the valleys we will see lower to mid 80s.\n\nStarting Friday, the monsoon flow is forecast to re-develop once \nagain and will likely be with us through early next week. Scattered \nto numerous storms will occur over the mtns with mainly isolated to \nscattered storms over the plains (with better chances along the I-25 \ncorridor region). \n\nSome of the rain during this period will have the potential to be \nrather heavy (especially over the mtns), as guidance indicates we \nmay see some mid to upper level tropical cyclone moisture being \nadvected into the region. \n\nTemperatures most areas this weekend will be similar to the \ntemperatures during this upcoming mid week time period, although the \nmtn temps may be a somewhat cooler due the expected increase in \ncloudiness.\\/Hodanish",
